==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From the ending of the words ''[[quintuple]]'', ''[[sextuple]]''; from Latin ''[[-plus]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/tʌpəl/}}
* {{rhymes|ʌpəl}}
* {{IPA|/tuːpəl/}}
* {{rhymes|uːpəl}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{set theory}} A [[finite]] [[sequence]] of [[term]]s; equivalently, an [[ordered]] [[set]].
# {{computing}} A single [[row]] in a [[relational database]].
# {{computing}} A [[set]] of comma-separated [[value]]s passed to a program or operating system as a [[parameter]] to a [[function]] [[call]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|finite sequence of terms}} [[n-tuple|''n''-tuple]] (''when the sequence contains'' n ''terms''), [[ordered pair]] (''when the sequence contains exactly two terms''), [[triple]] ''or'' [[triplet]] (''when the sequence contains exactly three terms'')

====Related terms====
* [[ordered pair]]
* [[tuplet]]
* [[component]]

